  "_comment": "Wings loft outboard along -X with sweep toward +Z and dihedral toward +Y, so one definition serves both sides: the port copy is authored, the starboard copy is generated by reflecting X. Hardpoints hang under the wing at negative X and are unrotated, which points a gun or a nacelle the correct way without further thought. Tip sockets accept wings, so wing-on-wing chaining works and is the cheapest way to see the recursion for yourself.",
